# Each extended brief's task block is a byte pin: the round manifest carries its
# sha256 and character count, and `bench-run.mjs`'s manifest gate compares both
# before anything is wiped. The repo is authored on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the exact setting that rewrites an unattributed text
# file on checkout — so these rules are load-bearing, not tidiness. Named
# patterns, not `*`: only the frozen briefs are pins.
bench-brief-extended.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-extended-32.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-extended-33.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-extended-36.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-extended-48.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-swe-lite.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-swe-rebench.md text eol=lf
bench-brief-compounded.md text eol=lf
